&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Submittable, we are transforming how organizations create social impact. Our platform empowers thousands of mission-driven organizations, from nonprofits to government entities, to make a difference in their communities and beyond. In 2024, our innovative software helped organizations worldwide run &lt;strong&gt;30,000 programs&lt;/strong&gt;, welcomed &lt;strong&gt;1.2 million applicants&lt;/strong&gt;, and facilitated the distribution of &lt;strong&gt;more than $10 billion&lt;/strong&gt; in funding through our products on behalf of our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are on a mission to help organizations accelerate their impact, so we are proud to partner with organizations focused on Equity &amp;amp; Social Justice, Children &amp;amp; Education, Creative &amp;amp; Arts, Health &amp;amp; Wellness, Economic Justice &amp;amp; Opportunity, and Environment &amp;amp; Climate. At Submittable, technology and purpose converge, offering a unique opportunity to contribute to meaningful change.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an intern who already has real hands-on experience with AI tools like Claude and Gemini and is excited to put that experience to work on real business problems. You&#39;ll join our G&amp;amp;A team, partnering with People Ops, IT, Finance, and Accounting to spot repetitive, manual processes and turn them into AI-assisted or fully automated workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role from day one — you&#39;ll be embedded with real teams, solving real problems, and helping move active projects across the finish line. It&#39;s a great fit for a business-minded student who wants experience at the intersection of AI, operations, and process improvement, and who wants to see their work actually put to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with G&amp;amp;A, People Ops, IT, and Accounting to identify and develop AI automated solutions to support daily operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and pilot AI-powered workflows and tools using Claude, Gemini, and other AI platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help move existing AI and operations projects forward — from research and prototyping to testing and rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document new processes and create simple guides or playbooks so teams can adopt and maintain the tools you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather requirements from stakeholders across departments, test proposed solutions, and iterate based on feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track the impact of your work — time saved, errors reduced, processes streamlined — and report results to G&amp;amp;A leaders and key stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on ad hoc business operations projects and tasks as priorities shift across the G&amp;amp;A function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated hands-on expertise using AI tools such as Claude and Gemini to complete work — research, writing, workflow design, data tasks, and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to speak concretely about how you&#39;ve used AI tools to solve a real problem, not just that you&#39;ve experimented with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree; Juniors, Seniors, and graduate students are all encouraged to apply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-related majors preferred (e.g., Business Administration, Management Information Systems, Business Analytics, Accounting) — but strong candidates from other majors with genuine AI expertise are welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a resourceful mindset and comfort learning new software quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills; comfortable working cross-functionally with stakeholders across multiple departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and detail-oriented, with the ability to manage several small projects at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work independently while knowing when to loop in your manager or stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;University of Montana students preferred; students at other schools are welcome to apply as long as they can reliably commute to and from work in person at our Missoula office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework or project experience in business process improvement, data analytics, or operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI tools, Large Language Models (LLMs), APIs, and automation platforms such as Zapier or Power Automate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid Excel and/or Google Sheets skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior internship or work experience in HR, IT, or Accounting functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Internship Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Duration: Fall 2026 term, with the possibility of extending into spring based on performance and team need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: On-site at Submittable&#39;s Missoula, MT headquarters. University of Montana students preferred; open to students at other schools who can commute in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: $16–$18/hour, based on experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule flexibility available around class schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct mentorship from Submittable&#39;s IT &amp;amp; Operations Manager and exposure to leaders across G&amp;amp;A, HR, IT, and Accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to work on real AI initiatives with direct, visible business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are interested in every qualified candidate eligible to work in the United States; however, &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;we cannot accommodate scholastic or employment visas at this time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;. In addition, we are not able to consider applicants who reside in the following states: &lt;strong data-start=&quot;401&quot; data-end=&quot;551&quot;&gt;Alaska, Delaware, Hawaii, Louisiana, Maine, New Mexico, North Dakota, Oklahoma, Rhode Island, Vermont, Washington, West Virginia, and Wyoming.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
